          "confidence": 0.85,
          "synopsis": "Introduces the two-sample Mann-Whitney U test as a rank-based alternative, describing how to compare every observation in group A against group B and count checkmarks to obtain the test statistic W. Notes that W's sampling distribution is complicated but interpreted like t or z, with two-sided rejection for very large or small W. Shows jamovi output for an Independent Samples T-Test with the Mann-Whitney U option, giving U = 3 and p = 0.05556.",
          "pages": [
            267,
            268,
            269
          ],
          "figure_ids": [
            "fig_45ecdb7da7734b_2064_v2",
            "fig_45ecdb7da7734b_2073_v2"
          ],
